{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that observes the dispatch cycle and forwards events to a provider-agnostic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":". Unlike the gate-style plugins ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":"), analytics is an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"observer","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it watches actions flow by and emits events, but never blocks dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two surfaces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mapper (passive)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — App declares a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]"},{"type":"text","text":" closure once at registration. The plugin runs it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (explicit)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Screen views, identify\/alias\/reset, ad-hoc tracks, and opt-out toggling. For the things passive observation can’t cover cleanly."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plus optional "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"auto-identify","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": pass an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath and the plugin watches userID transitions across dispatches, firing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.identify"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.reset"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Library target","type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Provided implementations","type":"heading","anchor":"Provided-implementations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin ships with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" for previews and tests. For production Mixpanel integrations, the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package provides:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that forwards to the Mixpanel SDK and maps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" to native Mixpanel types."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a Mixpanel-flavored mock for previews."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For other backends (Amplitude, PostHog, Segment, custom), implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" Step 3, Path B."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Types","type":"heading","anchor":"Types"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"final class"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsState"},{"type":"text","text":" and an action enum typed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, AnalyticsState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (AnalyticsAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> AnalyticsAction?,","    service: any AnalyticsService,","    mapper: AnalyticsMapper<RootState, RootAction> = .none,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity<RootState>? = nil",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"final class"},{"text":" (not a struct) because it tracks pending fire-and-forget service calls so that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":" can deterministically await them — same reason ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndoPlugin"},{"text":" are classes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsState`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsState"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isOptedOut: Bool","    public var currentScreen: String?","    public internal(set) var lastIdentifiedUserID: String?","","    public init(isOptedOut: Bool = false, currentScreen: String? = nil)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — App-controlled privacy flag. While "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mapper events are dropped, explicit "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actions become no-ops, and auto-identify is paused."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — The most recent screen recorded via "},{"code":".screenView(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", auto-attached as the "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property on subsequent tracked events."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Set by the plugin (read-only from outside the module). Used to detect identity transitions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsAction`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsAction"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsAction: Sendable, Equatable {","    case track(AnalyticsEvent)","    case screenView(String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case alias(newID: String, previousID: String?)","    case reset","    case setOptedOut(Bool)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Convenience factories cover the common no-properties cases:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".screenView(\"Profile\")                    \/\/ properties: [:]",".identify(userID: \"u1\")                   \/\/ properties: [:]",".alias(newID: \"user-42\")                  \/\/ previousID: nil"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsEvent`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsEvent: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var name: String","    public var properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(_ name: String, _ properties: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [:])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsValue`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsValue"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Closed enum keeping the protocol provider-agnostic and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":". Each service adapter maps these cases to its native property type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsValue: Sendable, Equatable {","    case string(String)","    case int(Int)","    case double(Double)","    case bool(Bool)","    case date(Date)","    case array([AnalyticsValue])","    case dict([String: AnalyticsValue])","    case null","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Literal conformances keep call-sites clean:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let props: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [","    \"amount\": 5,           \/\/ .int","    \"tier\": \"pro\",         \/\/ .string","    \"active\": true,        \/\/ .bool","    \"ratio\": 0.5,          \/\/ .double","    \"tags\": [\"a\", \"b\"],    \/\/ .array","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsMapper%3CState-Action%3E"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wraps the declarative ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>: Sendable {","    public typealias Map = @Sendable (State, Action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","    public let map: Map","    public init(_ map: @escaping Map)","    public static var none: AnalyticsMapper { ... }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".none"},{"text":" is the default mapper for plugins that only use explicit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"text":" dispatches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsIdentity<State>`","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsIdentity%3CState%3E"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declarative source-of-truth for the active user’s identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsIdentity<State>: Sendable {","    public let userID: @Sendable (State) -> String?","    public let userProperties: @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(","        userID: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> String?,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","","    public init(","        userID keyPath: KeyPath<State, String?> & Sendable,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The KeyPath convenience init is the typical shape: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.auth.currentUserID)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsService` (protocol)","type":"heading","anchor":"AnalyticsService-protocol"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsService: Sendable {","    func track(_ event: AnalyticsEvent) async","    func identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]) async","    func alias(newID: String, previousID: String?) async","    func reset() async","    func flush() async","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Implementations own batching, retry, network failure handling, and offline queueing. The plugin invokes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset"},{"text":" fire-and-forget; only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush"},{"text":" is awaited.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`MockAnalyticsService`","type":"heading","anchor":"MockAnalyticsService"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No-op conformer for previews and development.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init()","    \/\/ All methods are no-ops.","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Action semantics","type":"heading","anchor":"Action-semantics"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`track(AnalyticsEvent)`","type":"heading","anchor":"trackAnalyticsEvent"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns an effect calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.track(event)"},{"text":", with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentScreen"},{"text":" auto-attached as the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen"},{"text":" property if the event doesn’t already specify one. Skipped entirely (returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":") when opted out. No state mutation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`screenView(String, properties:)`","type":"heading","anchor":"screenViewString-properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentScreen"},{"text":" to the given name ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"regardless of opt-out"}]},{"text":" (the screen state still progresses for when the user opts back in). Returns an effect calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.track"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"screen_view\""},{"text":" event whose properties include ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_name"},{"text":" plus any extras. Skipped (returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":") when opted out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`identify(userID:, properties:)`","type":"heading","anchor":"identifyuserID-properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.identify"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Use this when the app needs to force identity before the auto-identify keypath would observe the change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`alias(newID:, previousID:)`","type":"heading","anchor":"aliasnewID-previousID"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No state mutation. Returns an effect calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.alias"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Call once when an anonymous user signs up to link the anonymous distinct ID to the new user ID."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`reset`","type":"heading","anchor":"reset"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.reset()"},{"type":"text","text":". Runs even when opted out — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset"},{"type":"text","text":" is by definition a clean-slate operation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`setOptedOut(Bool)`","type":"heading","anchor":"setOptedOutBool"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"setOptedOut(true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Sets "},{"code":"isOptedOut = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", clears "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to clear server-side identity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setOptedOut(false)"},{"type":"text","text":" — Clears the flag without a service call. Auto-identify on the next dispatch will re-establish identity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Mapper semantics","type":"heading","anchor":"Mapper-semantics"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The mapper runs in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in. The plugin:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips entirely if the action is an "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (handled by "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already, no double-tracking)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips when "},{"code":"state.isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls "},{"code":"mapper.map(state, action)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and tracks each returned event via "},{"code":"service.track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" auto-attached as "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (unless the event already provides its own "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. The mapper closure is allowed to read freely from the post-reducer state — that’s deliberately what gets passed in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Auto-identify semantics","type":"heading","anchor":"Auto-identify-semantics"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When configured with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the plugin re-evaluates both the ","type":"text"},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closures each non-analytics dispatch and diffs the pair ","type":"text"},{"code":"(userID, userProperties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the last value sent to the service:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nil → \"u1\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (sign-in): updates "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:\"u1\", properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"\"u1\" → \"u2\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (account switch): updates both, fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:\"u2\", properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable userID, "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" content changed: updates "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"code":"service.identify(userID:, properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the new dictionary."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"\"u1\" → nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (sign-out): clears both, fires "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable userID and stable "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": no-op."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is re-evaluated every non-analytics dispatch; dictionary equality decides whether to re-fire ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This keeps derived people-properties (subscription tier, paywall entitlements, feature flags) in sync with state without any explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":".identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plumbing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When opted out, auto-identify is paused: neither ","type":"text"},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nor ","type":"text"},{"code":"lastIdentifiedProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is updated. Opting back in re-establishes identity correctly on the next dispatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Flushing","type":"heading","anchor":"Flushing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" awaits any pending fire-and-forget service calls spawned by ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Call this on app shutdown to avoid losing in-flight events:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await store.analyticsPlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Implementing an `AnalyticsService`","type":"heading","anchor":"Implementing-an-AnalyticsService"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin is provider-agnostic. Your conformer is responsible for translating ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into whatever the backend SDK expects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has five methods, all ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and non-throwing. Errors are the service’s responsibility: log them, queue for retry, drop them — whatever fits your backend’s reliability model. The plugin will not see them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A typical Mixpanel conformer holds a reference to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mixpanel.Instance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and translates ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". An Amplitude conformer holds an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Amplitude","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance and translates to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[String: Any]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note what the protocol does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" require: no opt-out flag (the plugin handles that), no super-property machinery for ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text